I've been trying to compile NH3.0 constantly for the last week, and have almost
suceeded in doing so.  I downloaded the source onto my ancient IBM-PC1 (don't
worry!--the poor old thing has a 286 card in it now, enough memory, etc to
compile everything...).   I'm using Turbo C verson 2.0, Turbo C's MAKE utility
(only two or three minor changes were needed to get the Makefile.tcc to work,
which was my only option since I do not have NDMAKE...).  I've also exhausted
just about every linker I own trying to link the thing.   I have a few 
questions/comments for all the rest of you who are still fighting with it or
have compiled a running copy.
 
Is Fish's TERMCAP.LIB _entirely_ necessary?  I was under the impression
that there was an option (TERMLIB, or something like that) which you could
set if you knew you _didn't_ have this library.  I have the libraries that
came with Nethack 2.2, but unfortunately, there was no library for the HUGE
model.   So I went into TERMCAP.C (I know, cheating...) and fixed the file
up so that it didn't give me undefined symbols (tgetstr, tgetnum, tgetent, etc)
when I linked the program.  I just hardcoded the TERM values.  Can anybody
steer me right on this one, and perhaps send me the TERMLIB(CAP)(whatever).ARC
file?

At this point, I've been able to comile the source with no problems.  I am
having trouble with the linking process, though.  I've head the warnings about
Turbo C's line of linkers (1.0, 1.1, 2.0) having fatal troubles with the
huge model.  I tried them anyway (the executables always hung the system upon
running them), and then started using a Microsoft linker.  The Microsoft
linker created a slightly larger file (insignificantly larger, actually). Upon
running the executable, however, I get a message saying that the "program
may not be compatible with the 80286 processor," and a "bad opcode at
[some address]." (error message is not exact in format, but you get the
idea...).  _Any_ help on that one would be wonderful---I'm stuck at that
point right now (I've had _plenty_ of siestas waiting for the thing to
compile over and over again with different options...).

Well, any advice?  Congratulations to anybody who actually got a Turbo C version
to work....and good luck to everyone else who's trying...I sure need some!!!

